            <div xml:id="d493">

                <pb facs="0500" n="488" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg488"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">585.61B1/583: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-07-18T16:00:00+02:00">July 18, 1941—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 19—8:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3084. Department’s 2661, 18th.<anchor n="32" xml:id="d493-f1"/> Foreign Office
                    stated orally this morning that British authorities concerned do not believe it
                    technically possible to obtain assent of contracting parties because the
                    majority are either enemies or unaccessible governments. They will forward
                    shortly an alternative proposal not to enforce the convention between
                    ourselves.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
